  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_0' aria-label=\" The Commissioner, Bruhat Bangalore Mahanagara Palike versus K.K. Umesh Kumar & Ors. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('0','2026','2026_7_101_112','2026INSC637'); ><font size='4'> <strong>THE COMMISSIONER, BRUHAT BANGALORE MAHANAGARA PALIKE<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>K.K. UMESH KUMAR & ORS. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 7 S.C.R. 101</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 637</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010001912026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : SANJAY KAROL<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, N KOTISWAR SINGH</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Issue arose whether the appellant can be held liable under the Motor Vehicles Act, 1988 for the injuries sustained by respondent no.1 that were caused due to the falling of a roadside tree on the vehicle by which the respondent no.1 was under the tree waiting for the rain to subside and then proceed further. Headnotes&dagger; Motor Vehicles Act, 1988 &ndash; Compensation &ndash; Claim petition &ndash; Falling of a tree on an auto, if would qualify as an accident for which claim can be filed &ndash; Respondent was traveling<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 11-06-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 8455/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Disposed off</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('0','2026','2026_7_101_112','2026INSC637','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a><